# rpmlint filters for ants-terminal (ANTS-3729).
#
# No flag wires this up: obs-build invokes plain `rpmlint --info <rpms>`
# (build-recipe-spec:364, no --rpmlintrc). rpmlint 2.x auto-loads any
# *-rpmlintrc it finds in /home/abuild/rpmbuild/SOURCES, which is exactly where
# OBS stages the package sources — see lint.py:_load_rpmlintrc. So the file only
# has to be committed alongside the spec; obs-submit.sh copies it there.

# E: branding-requires-unversioned hicolor-icon-theme
#
# A bug in rpmlint's BrandingPolicyCheck, not a packaging defect. The check
# matches an unversioned Requires against
#     (?P<name>\S+)-(?P<type>branding|theme)
# with re.match, which is unanchored at the end and whose \S+ is greedy — so
# "hicolor-icon-theme" reads as the generic branding package "hicolor-icon"
# plus "-theme". It then demands `Requires: hicolor-icon-theme = <version>`,
# which would be actively wrong here: pinning an icon theme to an exact version
# breaks the package on the theme's next update.
#
# Two things say this is the check misfiring rather than a policy we are
# ducking. The same source defines `re_icon_theme = (?P<name>\S+)-icon-theme`
# and never references it — the exemption was written and never wired in. And
# every shipped openSUSE package that installs hicolor icons carries the
# identical unversioned Requires (libgtk-3-0, libgtk-4-1, ModemManager, feh).
#
# The Requires stays: hicolor-icon-theme owns /usr/share/icons/hicolor/*/apps,
# which is why ANTS-3726 added it in the first place.
#
# Self-expiring: if rpmlint fixes the check, this filter stops matching and
# rpmlint reports `unused-rpmlintrc-filter`. That is the signal to delete it.
addFilter("branding-requires-unversioned hicolor-icon-theme")
